  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry forecast dominates the work week, with\ntemperatures soaring above seasonal norms.\n\nUpper ridge in the Gulf will slowly push northward towards Texas\nand Louisiana, before moving eastward into the Deep South this\nweek. Subsidence keeps the forecast dry. Even more noticeable is\na mid-October heatwave that sends high temperatures in the mid-\nto-upper 80s. Wednesday through Friday appear to be the warmest,\nwhere several spots could be flirting with 90 degrees. Dewpoints\nwill remain in the mid 60s much of this week, getting near 70 at\ntimes during the coast.\n\nIt's October, mind you.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Most significant cooldown of the season so far\nsettles in this weekend.\n\nSummer-like ridge finally gets pushed into the Atlantic by a\npotent upper trough that dives southward from the upper Midwest.\nThis pushes a dry cold front through the region, and the\nCarolinas are finally greeted with glorious fall air by the\nweekend. Highs only reach the mid 60s, while lows Saturday night\ndip into the low-to-mid 40s. Break out the pumpkin spice!",
